	(descr "Adafruit 9-DOF BNO085 STEMMA QT breakout (PID 4754). Plug-in daughterboard on 2x 1x6 female headers, rows 17.78mm (0.70in) apart, 2.54mm pitch. Board 25.9x23.36mm. Pad geometry verified against the vendor KiCad footprint MODULE_4754 in pcb/datasheets/4754.zip (JP1 y=+8.89 / JP2 y=-8.89, x=-6.35..+6.35). Carrier lands (THT sockets): bottom row pad1-6 = VIN/3Vo/GND/SCL/SDA/INT ; top row pad7-12 = BT/P0/P1/RST/DI/CS. 2026-07-31 FIX: pad2/pad3 were GND/3Vo (wrong) -> 3Vo/GND. SPI mode: SCK=SCL(4) MISO=SDA(5) MOSI=DI(11) CS=CS(12) + INT(6) + RST(10); PS1=P1(9) and PS0=P0(8) must both be high before reset (CEVA 1000-3927 note 5). 3Vo(2) is the module LDO output -> leave NC. Vendor FP also has M2.5 holes at (+-10.16,+-8.89); omitted here since the module is retained by the sockets.")
	(tags "adafruit bno085 imu breakout 2x1x6")
